        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lee Tamahori, Robert Redford, Pete Dexter, Nick Nolte, Jennifer Connelly, Chazz Palminteri, Michael Madsen, Chris Penn, Melanie Griffith, Andrew McCarthy, Treat Williams, John Malkovich\n- Films: Once Were Warriors, Die Another Day, Mulholland Falls\n- Roles: filmmaker, actor, director, producer, businessman, environmentalist, philanthropist, writer\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Redford, born Charles Robert Redford Jr. on August 18, 1936, is an American actor, director, producer, businessman, environmentalist, and philanthropist.\n- Lee Tamahori was born on 17 June 1950 and is a New Zealand filmmaker.\n- Lee Tamahori is best known for directing the 1994 film Once Were Warriors and the 2002 James Bond film Die Another Day.\n- Mulholland Falls is a 1996 American neo-noir crime thriller film directed by Lee Tamahori and written by Pete Dexter.\n- Mulholland Falls stars Nick Nolte, Jennifer Connelly, Chazz Palminteri, Michael Madsen, Chris Penn, Melanie Griffith, Andrew McCarthy, Treat Williams, and John Malkovich.",
